hadiths[76]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1499","Muhammad bin Shuaib narrates: I asked Imam Uza'i and Saeed bin Abdul Aziz about this, and they both said: Consider the part of the Imam's prayer that you have found to be the first part of your prayer."
"1500","Hasan al-Basri narrates: When the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill for ten days, Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) led the people in prayer."
"1501","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: Whoever prays in the lead of the Imam, the recitations of the Imam will be counted as his recitations. This tradition is rejected, its narrator Sahl bin Abbas is obsolete."
"1502","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: Whoever is praying in the lead of the Imam, the recitation of the Imam will count as his recitation. A narrator named Abul Hasan has narrated it as a rejected hadith and it is an illusion."
"1503","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) says about reciting the Imam's recitation: It is enough for you to recite the Imam's recitation."
"1504","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Holy Prophet (PBUH) said: Whoever has an Imam present, the recitations of the Imam will count as his recitations. This hadith is not authentic, Muhammad bin Abdarazi narrator is unique in narrating it and it is weak."
"1505","Sayyiduna Abu Dardaa (RA) narrates: I asked the Prophet (PBUH) whether recitation will be performed in every prayer. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Yes, a person belonging to the Ansar said: It has become obligatory. The narrator narrates: Sayyiduna Abu Darda turned to me and said: Because I was sitting closest to him among those present."
"1506","Sayyidah Umm Waraqa, may Allah be pleased with her, used to lead the Imamate (of women)."
"1507","Rita Hanafia narrates: Sayyida Aisha used to lead us, she used to stand among the women in the obligatory prayer."
"1508","Hujairah bint Hussain narrates: Sayyidah Umm Salama (RA) led us in Asr prayer, and she stood between us. The same hadith has been narrated in some other contexts, but there is some illusion in its authenticity, and some have opposed it."
"1509","Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading the people in prayer. A person recited in his lead. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished praying, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Who is trying to interrupt these surahs?” Imam Darqutani (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates: These words of the tradition, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade people from reciting in the lead of the Imam."
"1510","Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) recited Surah Al-Ala while performing the Zuhr prayer. (After finishing the prayer), the Prophet (PBUH) inquired which of you was reciting. A narrator named Shuba narrates, I asked Qatadah: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disapprove of this, he replied that if you had disapproved of it, you would have forbidden it."
"1511","Sayyidna Masoor Bin Mukharama (RA) narrates: I saw Sayyidna Umar (RA) praying even though his wound was bleeding."
"1512","Sa'sa' bin Suhan narrates: Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said Takbeer five times, four times, and seven times in Iraq (in the funeral prayer). He has stated this: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said Takbeer (in the funeral prayer) eleven times, nine times, seven times, six times, five times, four times."
"1513","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated in Surah The narrator narrates: It is narrated only by a narrator named Hafs."
"1514","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite this in the Sajdah recitation. \My face is bowed before the One who created it"," gave it hearing and sight by His help and power.\"""""
"1515","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, Sayyidna Dawud (peace be upon him) prostrated here because of repentance, and we prostrate because of gratitude."
"1516","This hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission, which is about this prostration which is in the hundredth chapter of Prophet Dawud (peace be upon him) who performed this prostration as a repentance, and we perform this prostration as a sign of gratitude."
"1517","Saeed bin Jubayr narrates: He heard Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrating this."
"1518","Sa'ib bin Yazid narrates: Syedna Uthman Ghani (RA) recited 100 verses on the pulpit and then got down and recited Sajdah."
"1519","Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates: One day the Holy Prophet (PBUH) was delivering a sermon to us. There is an event of repentance and I see that you people are ready to prostrate, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came down from the pulpit and he prostrated, so we also prostrated."
"1520","Sayyiduna Amr bin As, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: The Holy Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, taught him fifteen places in the Holy Qur'an where prostration is performed, three of them are in detailed surahs, and two are prostrations in the Hundred-Rah Hajj."
"1521","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aamir Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: I asked: O Messenger of Allah, are there two prostrations in Hajj? He said yes, if you do not pay them then do not recite this surah."
"1522","Abdullah bin Tha'albah narrates: I saw Sayyiduna Umar, may God bless him and grant him peace, he performed two prostrations in Surah Hajj. The narrator narrates: I inquired whether in the morning prayer? He answered yes, in the morning prayer."
"1523","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (and with him) the jinn, humans and trees prostrated in the last verse of Surah Najam."
"1524","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated while reciting Surah Najm, and the Muslims and polytheists also prostrated (with him)."
"1525","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) recited this Surah, Al-Najm, and he prostrated in it."
"1526","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I have recited Sajdah in Surah Al-Anshaqaq and Surah Al-Alak following the example of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1527","Al-Khari bin Zayd narrates the statement of his father Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit Ansari: I recited Surah Najm in front of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and none of us prostrated. A narrator named Abu Sakhr narrates: I followed Umar bin Abdul Aziz and Abu Bakr bin Hazm (performed the prayer in which they recited this Surah), but they both did not recite Sajdah."
"1528","Abu Ja'afar narrates: The Holy Prophet saw a person who was imperfect, so he went into prostration."
"1529","Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (RA) narrates: Whenever the Prophet (PBUH) was happy, he (PBUH) would go into prostration to thank Allah."
"1530","Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (RA) narrates: Whenever the Prophet (PBUH) was in a happy situation or he (PBUH) was happy about something, he used to go into Sajdah."
"1531","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: This completes the prayer."
"1532","Jabir bin Yazid narrates the following statement from his father: I joined the Holy Prophet in his Hajj, I performed the morning prayer in the mosque of Khaif following him. When they went, both of them were trembling. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired why you two did not pray with us. They said, O Messenger of Allah, we had already prayed in our residence. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Do the Yesanah, when you have prayed in your residence, then you come to the mosque where the prayer is being offered with the congregation, then offer the prayer with the people, it will become a nafl prayer for you."
"1533","This tradition has been narrated along with some other isnads, but these words are added in it: One of them said: O Messenger of Allah! If you pray for forgiveness for us, then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Allah has forgiven you.\"""""
"1534","Jabir bin Yazid narrates the statement of his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered the Fajr prayer in Mina. When he finished the prayer, he saw two men behind the people. He called both of them. They were both trembling. He inquired why you did not offer the prayer with the people. They both said: We had already offered the prayer in our residence. He said: \You should do Asana when a person has offered the prayer in his residence and then he is the imam.\"" If he performs congregational prayer along with the Imam"," then it will become nafl for him."""
"1535","The same hadith is narrated along with some other isnads, but it contains these words: \So you people should pray with him and declare it as a Nafl prayer.\"" Some other narrators have narrated a tradition contrary to it."""
"1536","Jabir bin Yazid narrates the statement of his father: I prayed in the footsteps of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. When he finished the prayer, he saw two men behind the people. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do this. When a person has prayed in his home and then he comes to the Imam, he should offer the prayer with the Imam and the prayer he prayed in his home should be considered as Nafl."
"1537","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates a tradition similar to this regarding the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): However, it contains these words: \It will become a Nafl for both of you and what you performed in your residence will be an obligatory prayer.\"" This tradition along with some other isnaads has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him)."""
"1538","This tradition along with some other isnads is narrated by Jabir bin Yazid from his father."
"1539","This tradition along with some other isnaads has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Jabir bin Yazid."
"1540","The same hadith is related to Jabir bin Yazid in the same manner as the hadith of Shu'ba."
"1541","Basr bin Muhjan narrates this statement of his father: Once he was sitting with the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, got up and offered the prayer. When he came back, Sayyiduna Muhjan was sitting in his place. Aren't you a Muslim? He said yes! O Messenger of Allah, but I had prayed in my house, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them, when you come, pray with the people, even if you have already prayed. These words of the hadith are from Imam Malik, and its meaning is close."
"1542","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Do not perform the (same) obligatory prayer twice in a day."
"1543","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"1544","Ghulam Sulaiman, the slave of Sayyida Maimunah (RA) narrates: One day, I attended the service of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA), he was sitting in the court and the people were performing Asr prayer at that time. I said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman! People are praying? He said: I have performed the prayer (now I am not performing this prayer with the people) because I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: An obligatory prayer will not be performed twice in a day."
"1545","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform eleven rak'ahs between the time he finished the Isha prayer and the time when the morning prayer came. In them, he would say salam after every two rak'ahs and he would make them stand by one rak'ah. If so, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would get up and perform two short rak'ahs, then he would lie down on his right side until the muezzin came to call him for prayer, and he would accompany him. Various narrators have narrated this incident with a lack of words."
"1546","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The nawafl of the night and the day shall be paid by dudu."
"1547","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Nawafs of the night and the day will be paid in two."
"1548","Sayyidna Matal Radiyallahu Anhu narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Nafl) Prayer will be performed two by two. After praying two rakats, you will sit in Tashahhud, show humility and raise your hands and say Ya Allah, Ya Allah. Whoever does not do this (his prayer) will be incomplete. The same hadith has been narrated from Sayyidna Fazl bin Abbas with reference to another chain of transmission."
"1549","Yasar narrates: Once, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) saw me praying (Nafal) in the morning after becoming righteous, and while hitting me with pebbles, he said, \O Jesus! How many rakaat have you performed? I replied"," \""I don't remember.\"" He said: \""You don't understand. Once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us and we were performing the Nawafil prayer. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) expressed his great displeasure at us and said: Let all those present convey this to those who are not present: After being righteous in the morning"," only two rak'ahs (Sunnah) can be offered."""
"1550","Yasar narrates: Once Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) saw me reciting Nawafil after I became righteous in the morning, and Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said: O Yasar! Once, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us and we were performing this Nawafil prayer at that time, so he said: All people should convey this to those who are not present."
"1551","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: After the morning prayer, no prayer can be offered except two rak'ahs of the Sunnah."
"1552","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: Once the Prophet (PBUH) found some people absent during the prayer (in congregation) and inquired: Why did those people not participate in the prayer? So the people told him that he had some work to do, so he said: A person who lives in the neighborhood of the mosque prays only in the mosque. These words of the tradition are from the narrator named Ibn Mukhlid: while the narrator named Abu Hamid has quoted these words: A person who hears the call to prayer and does not come (to the mosque) does not pray, but if there is an excuse, then (the ruling is different)."
"1553","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Huraira: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that the person who lives in the neighborhood of the mosque prays only in the mosque."
"1554","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Whoever lives in the neighborhood of the mosque and hears the muezzin giving the call to prayer and does not come (to the mosque to offer prayers) without an excuse, then his prayer is not performed."
"1555","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever hears the call to prayer and does not respond to it (i.e. does not come to the mosque to pray in congregation), his prayer is not performed, but if there is an excuse, then (the ruling is different)."
"1556","This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, while some narrators have quoted it as a marfu' hadith."
"1557","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: He who listens to the call to prayer and does not have an excuse to obey him (i.e. going to pray in congregation), people asked what is meant by an excuse? He said: Fear or illness (the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, then Allah will not accept the prayer that this person has offered (in his home)."
"1558","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a person forgets a prayer and then remembers that prayer while he is performing another prayer, he should first perform his current prayer, when he is finished with it, then perform the prayer that he forgot."
"1559","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) says: When a person forgets a prayer and then remembers that prayer when he is in the lead of the Imam, he should perform the prayer followed by the Imam."
"1560","Some narrators have narrated it as a marfu' hadith, but these narrators are delusional about it."
"1561","Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: Praying while sitting has half the reward of praying while standing, and praying while lying down has half the reward of praying while sitting."
"1562","Sayyidna Jabir (RA) narrates: Once the Prophet (PBUH) was riding a horse in Madinah, and he was injured by a palm trunk, as a result of which his foot was injured. He stayed in the house of Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa. When we came to your service (the next time), you were performing the obligatory prayer at that time. We stood behind you, so you indicated to us that we should sit down. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer, he said: Follow the Imam."
"1563","The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, the word, Nafl, is not mentioned in it."
"1564","Ibrahim bin Ubaid narrates: I attended the service of Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, and I found his companions sitting and leading the prayer. When they had finished praying, I asked them about it. Pray standing and when he prays sitting, you should also pray sitting."
"1565","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): “Whoever forgets to pray, the time to perform it will be when he remembers it.”"
"1566","Sayyiduna Jubayr bin Mut'am Radiyallahu Anhu narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: O Banu Abd Manaf, if you become the supervisor of this task, then you should never prevent anyone from circumambulating the House of Allah and offering prayers, regardless of the time of day or night."
"1567","Sayyidna Jubayr bin Mut’im (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH): O Banu Abd Manaf (the narrator is doubtful, perhaps these are the words) O children of Qusay: Do not prevent anyone from circumambulating the House of Allah and offering prayers here, whatever part of the day or night."
"1568","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: O Banu Abd Manaf: Be careful not to prevent anyone from praying at this House of Allah, no matter what time of the day or night."
"1569","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Banu Abdul Munaf, do not prevent anyone from circumambulating this House of Allah, whatever the time of the day or night."
"1570","Nafi bin Jubayr narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in reference to his father: O Banu Abd Manaf, do not forbid anyone who is praying near this House of Allah, whatever the time of the day or night."
"1571","Mujahid narrates: When Sayyiduna Abu Zar Ghafari, may God be pleased with him, came to Makkah, he held the door frame of the Kaaba and said: Whoever knows me knows me, but whoever does not know me (let him know) I am Jandab (and my surname is Abu Dhar). And no (Nafal) prayer can be performed from the time of the Asr prayer until the sunset, although the ruling of Makkah is different."
"1572","Sayyiduna Jubayr bin Mut'ayim (RA) narrates: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying, O Banu Abdul Muttalib! You should not prevent anyone from praying at this House of Allah, no matter what time of the day or night."
"1573","Nafi bin Jubayr narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this, O Banu Abd Manaf! O Banu Hashim, if this matter were in Your power, I would never prevent a person circumambulating this house (and anyone praying near it) from (circumcising or offering prayers) at any time of the night or day."
"1574","This tradition is narrated along with another document, but it contains these words. \You shall not prevent anyone from circumambulating this House of Allah at any time of the day or night."""
